and the impact on people might be looked at in terms of public stigma, what happens when you're the butt of stereotypes and prejudice or self-stigma, what happens when you internalize it? And we pretty much agree that the stigma of mental illness is the same category as racism and sexism and ageism. And just as that's a priority in American culture, so it falls to mental health and other. their health conditions. So how does stigma prevent people from getting the care that they need? I know that you've written about that.

