your friends and your neighbors, and maybe the same thing is happening right now with people who have mental illness, right? I mean, how do we change that? Amen. So some stigmas are obvious. Racial stigma is mostly obvious. You can tell by skin color. Sexism is mostly obvious. You can tell by body type. Old age is obvious. You can tell by gray hair. You can't pretty much tell the stigma of mental illness. And in that way, it's a lot like the stigma LGBTQ is what's happened in our lifetime is the stigma LGBTQ has changed hugely, improved greatly. And they'll get me wrong, we still got a long way to go.

